       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day for a 70 kg adult. That is a potentially lethal dose, well into the range where acute liver failure is expected. No indication I know of supports a dose like this.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). A lower maximum is often used for chronic use or low body weight.\n- **Enter a different regimen**, if you meant something else, such as 500 mg or 650 mg per dose.\n- **Treat this as a possible overdose**, if the intent is related to ingestion or poisoning. That calls for poison control and an N-acetylcysteine protocol, not a scheduled acetaminophen order.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason I'm not seeing, please discuss it with pharmacy. They can review it and enter the order through their own verification process. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
